+# Q3 revenue drop: East region
+
+East had the largest percentage fall from Q2 to Q3 of any region. Its revenue went from $333,747.57 to $234,325.08, a drop of 29.79% ($99,422.49). The next-worst region was North at −4.33%. Ledger Pro accounts for most of the drop: its East revenue fell from $106,520.77 to $23,015.24 (−$83,505.53, about 84% of the region's decline). The cause was volume, not price: completed Ledger Pro orders in East fell from roughly 100 a month in April–June to 22–28 a month in July–September, while unit prices stayed about the same. Ledger Pro recovered in Q4. Revenue counts completed rows only, as units × unit_price, and refunds (negative units) are netted in. Note that Q4 includes rows dated after today (2026-10-18).
+
+| Quarter | East revenue |
+|---------|-------------:|
+| Q1 | $333,565.48 |
+| Q2 | $333,747.57 |
+| Q3 | $234,325.08 |
+| Q4 | $305,168.76 |
